      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This was the biggest glaring issue I noticed with my initial use. Being on Index, I have my left thumbstick click mapped to my A button, which makes it super easy, quick, and intuitive to toggle gestures on and off.\nWhat used to be one action, now takes two actions, both of which take longer to do. This will be incredibly frustrating. I think the simplest solution would be to maintain a dedicated gesture toggle action which can be mapped through the Steam Input. This would allow a legacy option for those who find the new system to be much harder to control (which goes against one of the base goals of the new system).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5f083a840fa52b04645f911f",
      "author": {
        "_id": "58d2df84430f4652e88c5666",
        "alias": "Razzmatazz Bee",
        "aliasID": "65c27b0eed6eefce4c7d1c3c",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/4b44d3d0afb2c67cc49d31dfa6572c9c.png",
        "created": "2017-03-22T20:33:08.848Z",
        "name": "Mimi",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5ed571497ee72a2434704a15",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2020-07-10T09:53:08.685Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
