        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "any toggle you turn on in the new menu will not only lock it on, but it will sync the parameter for late joiners as well.\ntoggle sets a parameter to a value and holds it. when toggled off it resets it to 0.\nnot only that, but because you can send actual animator parameters now, you can set your animator up so, say you use a button (a button does what a toggle does, but doesn't hold it. you press it to momentarily make a parameter a value, then back to 0) to move the animator into a state with a hat on. even if that parameter is now 0 you will still have the had on.\nyou can do what you want, but much much better using using the action menu, so much better that if you take the time, you can even make a very long animation using music and synced visuals semi synced for late joiners by breaking it into a state machine with many entry points that a later joiner could join and slot right into, as granular as you want to spend the time making it",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
