      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58d2df84430f4652e88c5666|full_name}: The one button toggles worked just fine in the Action Emote circle, however I'm talking about the ones have their own mini-menu (like multiple dances into one toggle) where you do have to keep your finger/hand pressing in order to keep it playing.  You get more animations for the real-estate but you've lost that ability to keep them on just like you mentioned.\nIt feels like they're trying to do too much with such a limited space.  What I expected when using the Action menu was: Press, and BAM, emote toggles all around.  Instead it's a two step action: Press, Emote Toggle Menu and then find the Emote you want (unless it's nested into yet another circle).  \nThe redundancy of the emojis and putting settings and such when I just want to use the \"Action\" menu just seems to crowd the fluidity on the user's side.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
